      "results": [
        {
          "ruleId": "cron_slot_evidence_not_in_tree_and_conflicts_with_3292",
          "level": "warning",
          "message": {
            "text": "The 23:17Z move rests on a 14-night measurement (slots fired 22:38-02:36Z) that is quoted in the commit message and header but not in the tree. The tree holds a different measurement: .github/workflows/qwen-story-daily.yml:15-27 (#3292) records schedule events dispatched 3h51m-6h49m late and calls the delay a moving target that is growing. Applied to a 23:17Z slot that is 03:08Z-06:06Z. The arithmetic is right (critical path b2-gpu 90 + measure-cleanroom-gpu 10 + cleanroom-gpu 5 = 105 min; 02:36Z + 1h45 = 04:21Z, 24 min margin; publish path 10+80+5 = 95 min), but a start after 03:00Z ends past 04:45Z and reads not_measured. Direction is conservative, never a false green."
          },
          "properties": {
            "grounding": "cited",
            "citation": ".github/workflows/qwen-story-daily.yml:15-27; .github/workflows/release-lanes-nightly.yml:47-150 timeout-minutes; .github/workflows/b2-gpu.yml:59",
            "failure_scenario": "A night where the 23:17Z event dispatches at 03:30Z: the run ends no earlier than 05:15Z in the worst chain, the train reads at 04:45Z, and the three lanes read not_measured that night. Not a wrong verdict, a missing one.",
            "precision_class": "advisory"
          }
        },
        {
          "ruleId": "stale_secret_wording_in_release_lanes_sh",
          "level": "note",
          "message": {
            "text": "scripts/release/release_lanes.sh:32 (header) and :245 (the not_measured reason string) still say repository secret INFRA_ACTIONS_READ; after this commit it is an environment secret of infra-read. The delta rewrites the workflow header only. Wording only; the self-test row at :394 matches on the INFRA_ACTIONS_READ token, which is unchanged, so no behaviour breaks. Leaving it matches the ruling to change nothing else."
          },
          "properties": {
            "grounding": "cited",
            "citation": "scripts/release/release_lanes.sh:32,245",
            "failure_scenario": "An operator reading the lane reason on a not_measured night is told to look for a repository secret and does not find the environment one.",
            "precision_class": "advisory"
          }
        },
        {
          "ruleId": "environment_claim_verified",
          "level": "note",
          "message": {
            "text": "Claim 2 holds. gh api shows environment infra-read with custom branch policies, allowed branches [main], and secret INFRA_ACTIONS_READ present. measure-cleanroom-cpu is the only reader of secrets.INFRA_ACTIONS_READ in the tree (git grep). A refused or failed measure job writes no verdict output, so cleanroom-cpu (if: always() && verdict in green,red) is skipped, and release_lanes.sh header lines 12-18 read a skipped lane job as not_measured. Scheduled runs use the default branch, so the nightly is allowed. One consequence: a workflow_dispatch from a non-main branch shows a failed measure job in the run, with the lane reading not_measured."
          },
          "properties": {
            "grounding": "measured",
            "command": [
              "gh",
              "api",
              "repos/paiml/aprender/environments/infra-read/deployment-branch-policies"
            ],
            "exit_code": 0,
            "precision_class": "advisory"
          }
        },
        {
          "ruleId": "delta_is_exactly_the_ruled_scope",
          "level": "note",
          "message": {
            "text": "git diff 92dc2ee2ef..4ad15e209d is one file, 12 insertions and 6 deletions: header comment lines, the cron expression, and one environment: line. No job, needs, if:, timeout or run line changed, so every gate is kept. actionlint exits 0. --self-test 69 ok 0 broke and --mutants 25/25 killed, re-run. check_pr_review_receipt --match-path, --match-crux-surface and --match-mutation-trigger all rc 1 on the file. Pre-existing and outside the delta: scripts/check_release_scripts_derive_identity.sh is red on release_lanes.sh from an earlier round, fixed in a separate follow-up PR."
          },
          "properties": {
